<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaHodaah [The Blessing of Thanksgiving] — Halachah 6<br>Part 3 (§§ 24–36 / Oaseyos כד–לו)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE · Based on <span class="lr">LM I:24</span> (<i>Amtza'isa D'Alma</i>)</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 24 — Yaakov's Dream at Bais Kel: The Ladder, the Stone, and the Obstructer</div>
<div class="p"><span class="v">"He encountered the place"</span> — the aspect of the striking of the pursuit against the obstructer, the aspect of <span class="h">Keser</span>, called "place," as explained in the above <span class="h">Torah</span> on the verse <span class="v">"blessed is the glory of Hashem from His place."</span> From there is the essential root of all places in the world, drawn forth and coming into being through many <span class="h">tzimtzumim</span>. This is the aspect of what is explained (<span class="lr">LM II:83</span>): the ultimate knowledge is that we do not know — the aspect of "the Place of the world," etc.; see there.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He lodged there, for the sun had set"</span> — the setting of the sun is the aspect of the withdrawal and prevention of the light through the obstructer. The sun is the light of intellect pursuing to grasp the light, but the obstructer prevents it, as above. Therefore <span class="v">"he lodged there"</span> — the essential sleep is this aspect. By day, through <span class="h">tefilah</span>, Torah, and <span class="h">mitzvos</span> with joy, the mental faculties are drawn through the striking of the pursuit against the obstructer, etc. But from the exertion they must withdraw after <span class="h">tefilah</span> — only a residual impression remains. Afterward, toward evening, they withdraw completely, as explained in the <span class="h">kavanos</span> of the Arizal. This is: <span class="v">"he lodged there, for the sun had set"</span> — Yaakov saw it was impossible now to perceive the mental faculties in completeness, for the sorting from the Chambers of Exchange had not yet been completed. Therefore <span class="v">"he lodged there."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He lodged there"</span> also alludes to the exiles, as our Sages say. From there all exiles come — through the corruptions of the generations who do not properly sort from the Chambers of Exchange, many causing damage, <span class="h">Rachmana litzlan</span>. Because of this, even the great <span class="h">tzadikim</span>, the forefathers, cannot perceive as they wish. Therefore he was compelled to lodge — the aspect of sleep and cessation — until he sorts properly. This is: <span class="mx">"one who comes to purify is told: wait!"</span> — said regarding every Jew wanting to purify himself, as explained (<span class="lr">LM I:6</span>). And likewise regarding the <span class="h">tzadik</span> laboring to purify Israel.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He took from the stones of the place and set them at his head"</span> — he took and sorted from the stones of the place: the sorting of letters and sparks — holy stones fallen into the Chambers of Exchange (= stumbling-stones): <span class="v">"the holy stones are poured out"</span> etc. The <span class="h">tzadik</span> sorts the good stones (= holy stones, the letters of Torah) from the Chambers of Exchange, and <span class="v">"set them at his head"</span> — binding them into the head and intellect.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He lay down in that place"</span> — he fell asleep amidst words of Torah. This alludes to every person: when one sees he is being prevented as he is being prevented, he must bind words of Torah in his thought, remove his thought from evil musings, and bind words of Torah in his thought until he falls asleep amidst words of Torah — the essential sorting from the Chambers of Exchange. This is the aspect of <span class="h">teshuvah of corresponding weight</span> — the essential <span class="h">tikun</span> of the damage of the <span class="h">bris</span> (= the damage of thought), whose entire <span class="h">tikun</span> is specifically through this, as brought regarding the teaching of our Sages (in <span class="lr">LM I:27</span>, the <span class="h">Torah</span> "<span class="h">R'tzitzah</span>"; see there).</div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="v">"he lay down in that place"</span> — <span class="v">"that place"</span> specifically, where he encountered (= the obstructer). There specifically he bound his thought with a strong bond until he slept. Every person must do likewise: even though he sees his thought is being obstructed as it is obstructed, he must do his part — to flee from evil thoughts and bind his thought to the aspect of "the Place of the world." Even though he cannot yet perceive or understand anything from there, his thought should remain bound there through the stones of the place (= the letters of Torah), until he falls asleep amidst words of Torah — the aspect of <span class="v">"he lay down in that place,"</span> as above.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He dreamt, and behold, a ladder set upon the earth, its top reaching the heavens"</span> etc. He saw this is the totality of man's service in this world: one must descend to this physical earth where the Chambers of Exchange cling, sort from there, and ascend through all the above ascents by means of this ladder whose top reaches the heavens — the aspect of the upper <span class="h">Prisah</span> (= <span class="h">Keser</span>), through which all perception of the nine chambers is accomplished, as above.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Sulam</span> [ladder] alludes to this, for <span class="h">sulam</span> in <span class="h">gematria</span> equals <span class="h">kol</span> [voice] — the aspect of <span class="v">"the voice is the voice of Yaakov."</span> Through this comes all the Jew's overpowering against all the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> and Chambers of Exchange, all encompassed in Esav: <span class="mx">"when the voice is the voice of Yaakov, the hands are not the hands of Esav"</span> — he has no power.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"The voice is the voice of Yaakov"</span> — two voices. The essential completeness is joy, through which all perception of the <span class="h">Ain Sof</span> light, as above. The essential joy is voices: the above five voices — <span class="v">"voice of joy and voice of gladness"</span> etc.; <span class="v">"the joy of Hashem is your strength"</span> — <span class="v">"He gives His voice a voice of strength"</span> etc. But due to the overpowering of exile (whose core is the exile of the soul, essentially through the overpowering of sadness, from which all troubles come, <span class="h">Rachmana litzlan</span>) — one must cry out greatly every day. The essential voice of crying out is to merit leaving sadness, from sorrow to joy: <span class="v">"they cried out"</span> etc., <span class="v">"they rejoiced when they were stilled"</span> etc. (in Mizmor <span class="h">Hodu</span>). One must cry out greatly to merit joy, which is the essential thing.</div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="v">"the voice is the voice of Yaakov"</span> — two voices: the voice of joy and the voice of crying to merit joy. One is deficient [in spelling] and one is full, as is known. The voice of crying is deficient — not completeness; the essential completeness is the voice of joy. But one must cry over his troubles (= deficiencies, whose source is the deficiency of joy). Therefore <span class="v">"the voice is the voice of Yaakov"</span> — one deficient, one full. All this is alluded to in the ladder Yaakov saw (= <span class="h">kol</span> in <span class="h">gematria</span>) — the aspect of voices, whose essence is the voice of joy, through which comes the essential ascent from earth to heaven: <span class="v">"a ladder set upon the earth, its top reaching the heavens,"</span> as above.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Behold, angels of G-d ascending and descending on it"</span> — the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>: <span class="v">"bless Hashem, all His angels"</span> etc. (holy Zohar). Ascending and descending — one must ascend and descend many times: entering and exiting, running and returning. The work is not for one day or one year. One must ascend and descend many times, each according to his level, until he merits the nine chambers. Therefore one needs every day <span class="h">hisbodedus</span>, conversation, many cries, etc. The essential thing: to overpower every day and at all times with joy, as explained extensively, and as explained (<span class="lr">LM II:25</span>) and elsewhere regarding <span class="h">hisbodedus</span> — concluding: <span class="mx">"the rest of the day he should be in joy"</span> — as above.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Behold, Hashem was standing over him"</span> etc. — only through this one perceives His G-dliness (= the <span class="h">Ain Sof</span> light perceived through the nine chambers merited through joy). <span class="v">"I am Hashem, the G-d of Avraham... the land upon which you lie — to you I shall give it and to your seed"</span> — the essential attainment is only in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, where the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> is — encompassing all ten levels of holiness (= the nine chambers, the totality of the mind, with <span class="h">Keser</span>, the tenth level, the <span class="h">Kodesh Kadashim</span>).</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Your seed shall be like the dust of the earth"</span> — the dust of the earth is the totality of the physical place in its utmost physicality. Its root is the Supernal Place (= the obstructer, "the Place of the world"), from which this physical place derives — where all trial and free will reside. Due to the corruptions, the Chambers of Exchange clung to the physical place: <span class="v">"cursed is the ground for your sake; in sadness you shall eat it."</span> All the forefathers labored in this <span class="h">tikun</span>. But Avraham and Yitzchak — their beds were not complete (Esav and Yishmael came from them, from whom all exiles come = sadness), the earth not yet purified. But Yaakov's bed was complete — therefore he was blessed: <span class="v">"your seed shall be like the dust of the earth"</span> specifically; <span class="v">"you shall burst forth to the west and east and north and south"</span> — an inheritance without boundaries, as our Sages say. He merited rectifying the sin of Adam HaRishon most — the final <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> will be in the aspect of Yaakov, as our Sages say. He raises the dust of the earth to the root of the Place (= "the Place of the world").</div>

<div class="p">Therefore he was told: <span class="v">"your seed shall be like the dust of the earth, and you shall burst forth"</span> etc. Wherever Israel descends, he will sort and raise them: <span class="v">"if your outcasts are at the end of the heavens, from there He will gather you."</span> All this alludes to the righteous redeemer who will emerge from him — illuminating in every generation, in all the seed of Israel, to gladden and strengthen them with his great power and deep counsel, until he raises them from all terrible places. From all of them he will gather, raise, and rectify: <span class="v">"you shall burst forth to the west and east"</span> etc. — <span class="v">"let the redeemed of Hashem say so... from the lands He gathered them,"</span> as above.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Through you all families of the earth shall be blessed, and through your seed"</span> — the above blessings received by sorting from the Chambers of Exchange through joy (= voice, the ladder). <span class="v">"Behold, I am with you"</span> — the ascent of <span class="h">Malchus</span>, His <span class="h">Shechinah</span>, which was in exile in the Chambers of Exchange. Through his service, he sorted from there. Hashem told him: <span class="v">"I am with you"</span> — always with him wherever he is. Through this comes the power to sort and raise His <span class="h">Malchus</span> — by knowing Hashem is with him even in the outer places, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>: <span class="v">"even when I walk in the valley of the shadow of death, I fear no evil, for You are with me."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"I shall guard you wherever you go"</span> — guarding the feet, the instruments of walking. <span class="v">"I shall return you to this land"</span> — from all descents and ascents, returning to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> (where the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> is, where the nine chambers are perceived). <span class="v">"I shall not abandon you"</span> etc. — our Sages expound: He promised regarding livelihood: <span class="v">"I have not seen a righteous person abandoned"</span> (Midrash Rabbah, Beraishis 69). He promised the blessing of the hands (= livelihood that Yaakov received from Yitzchak: <span class="v">"G-d shall give you from the dew of the heavens"</span>). For the great <span class="h">tzadikim</span> it is all one: through the blessing of livelihood they receive the blessing of intellect — their eating and livelihood is in such holiness that it itself is the blessing of intellect, receiving mind and intellect through their eating, as explained elsewhere.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Yaakov awoke from his sleep and said: 'Surely Hashem is in this place, and I did not know.'"</span> <span class="v">"I did not know"</span> — the ultimate knowledge that we do not know (= the Place, <span class="h">Keser</span>, the Arranger and Settler, the obstructer). Through this specifically comes the essential perception of His G-dliness — through the striking of the pursuit against the obstructer. Yaakov said: specifically through <span class="v">"I did not know"</span> (= the obstructer), he perceived His G-dliness: <span class="v">"Hashem is in this place."</span> Specifically through the obstructer — the prevention of knowledge until one settles — one grasps the <span class="h">Ain Sof</span> light.</div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="mx">"the Torah is sustained only in one who makes himself as if he does not know."</span> Specifically through the absence of knowledge (= the obstructer), one merits the perception of Torah (= the mind). (This is Rabbainu's <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> way: each time he would say he knows nothing at all, then afterward achieve awesome perceptions — many times throughout his life, as brought in Hilchos Tefillin 5 and elsewhere.) At every knowledge and perception there is the ultimate knowledge that we do not know. Afterward, specifically through having nullified himself and known he knows nothing — he perceives what he perceives, from the absence of knowledge to knowledge: <span class="v">"wisdom is found from nothing"</span> — from nothing specifically. Everything through the joy of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He was afraid and said: 'How awesome is this place!'"</span> — at the striking of the pursuit against the obstructer, there is the essential supernal <span class="h">yirah</span>: <span class="v">"Moshe hid his face, for he was afraid to gaze."</span> When the mind pursues to perceive, fear falls upon it from the obstructer. This is: <span class="v">"fear of Hashem is the beginning of knowledge"</span>; <span class="v">"the beginning of wisdom is fear of Hashem"</span> — <span class="h">Keser</span>, the obstructer, above the mind, obstructing it — the aspect of fear. Through this comes the essential perception of wisdom: <span class="v">"the beginning of wisdom is fear of Hashem; good understanding"</span> — specifically through the fear one perceives good understanding.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"This is none other than the house of G-d"</span> — the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>. He understood it is impossible to complete these perceptions except when the house of G-d is built — the final <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, built in his merit, as our Sages expound. He said <span class="v">"this is not"</span> — alluding to the destructions, as our Sages say. Even though he now perceives and sees — this is still not the ultimate perception, but only the house of G-d, the final <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>. Then everything will be rectified, the Chambers of Exchange sorted, and we will merit immense joy: <span class="v">"for with joy you shall go out."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Yaakov rose early in the morning"</span> — like the light of day, when all the above ascents are accomplished through <span class="h">tefilah</span>. <span class="v">"He took the stone... and poured oil upon its top"</span> — the holy anointing oil (= the mind), from which the <span class="h">menorah</span>-oil is drawn (= the <span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span>). All lights and perceptions (<span class="v">"the lamp of Hashem is the soul of man"</span>) are drawn only through the pursuit and the obstructer. The obstructer is the aspect of a stone — appearing to obstruct like a stone, preventing light. But in truth, through it comes the essential light: <span class="v">"He made darkness His hiding place"</span> (= <span class="h">Keser</span>, the obstructer). Our Sages expound: <span class="mx">"lest you say there is no light within — 'from the brightness before Him, His thick clouds passed'"</span> etc. Even physically, all fire-light is generated through striking specifically — Hashem gave understanding to Adam HaRishon on <span class="h">Motza'ai Shabbos</span> to take two stones, etc. This is: <span class="mx">"a tree that does not catch fire — they strike it"</span> etc. All deriving from the striking of the pursuit against the obstructer, from which the nine chambers are fashioned — not illuminated, etc. — higher than all lights, and specifically from there all lights in the world are drawn. Therefore the essential kindling of the lamps is at the time of the <span class="h">ketores</span>: <span class="v">"oil and incense gladden the heart."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"If G-d will be with me"</span> — <span class="h">Malchus</span>: <span class="v">"G-d is my King from of old"</span> — the above ascent of <span class="h">Malchus</span>. <span class="v">"He will guard me on this way"</span> — guarding <span class="h">Netzach-Hod-Yesod</span>, the instruments of walking. <span class="v">"He will give me bread to eat and a garment to wear"</span> — the blessing of the hands (= the blessing of intellect clothed in livelihood). "Bread" alludes to the bread of Torah; "garment" is the <span class="h">chaluka d'Rabbanan</span>, garments of the soul — all one for the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"I shall return in peace to my father's house"</span> — <span class="h">av</span> in wisdom. <span class="v">"I shall return"</span> specifically — from wherever he may be, he will return in peace to the intellect and wisdom (= <span class="v">"my father's house"</span>). Whether descending to the Chambers of Exchange — sorting and ascending to the intellect in peace. Or whether the intellect pursues — he will not break through, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>; through the Arranger and Settler, he returns in peace to the intellect, perceiving the <span class="h">Ain Sof</span> light in <span class="h">mati v'lo mati</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Hashem shall be my G-d"</span> — these perceptions are the essential drawing of His G-dliness. <span class="v">"This stone... shall be the house of G-d"</span> — encompassing all nine chambers with the <span class="h">Prisah</span>, where His G-dliness rests — in totality the ten levels of holiness (= the root of the Ten Utterances = the Ten Commandments). <span class="v">"All that You give me, I shall tithe"</span> — the secret of <span class="h">ma'aser</span> and <span class="h">ma'aser min hama'aser</span>. All for the blessing of intellect: from all bounty Israel receives, they must tithe to the <span class="h">Kohanim</span> and <span class="h">Levi'im</span>. The <span class="h">Kohanim</span>, with whom all blessings reside — through their service in the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> with joy, aroused by the <span class="h">Levi'im</span> engaged in song (= the ten types of melody, drawing joy), through which all the above <span class="h">tikunim</span> are accomplished. Therefore tithes flow through them to all Israel — the essential blessing being the blessing of intellect, encompassed in ten.</div>

<div class="p">This is stated in the Midrash HaNe'elam: <span class="mx">"ascending and descending on it, as it is said: 'we shall exult and rejoice in Him'"</span> — the ascending and descending is according to the joy in Him, through which all the above <span class="h">tikunim</span> are accomplished.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 25 — Yaakov's Battle with the Angel of Esav: Seizing Sorrow to Transform to Joy</div>

<div class="p">This is Yaakov's battle with the angel of Esav: <span class="v">"a man wrestled with him"</span> etc. Our Sages say this was the angel of Esav. Their entire battle was about the exiles — the man sought to prolong the exiles, wanting to overpower until, <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>, it would be impossible to leave. Since the end of the <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> is exceedingly hidden, they claim they will overpower until all hope is lost. Their essential overpowering is the exile of the soul — overpowering every Jewish soul, from which the general exile lengthens. The essential overpowering of the <span class="h">klipos</span> is through sadness.</div>

<div class="p">It was impossible to overpower them because one depends on the other: the more sadness overpowers, the more desires overpower; conversely, the more desires overpower, the more sadness overpowers. According to their overpowering, it is impossible to engage in <span class="h">tefilah</span> properly, ascending where the source of joy is. We would have nearly perished were it not that Hashem sends in every generation true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> who fight on our behalf.</div>

<div class="p">This is Yaakov's battle — from whom the essential holiness and joy of Israel begins: <span class="v">"let Yaakov exult, let Israel rejoice."</span> Yaakov is truth: <span class="v">"grant truth to Yaakov."</span> Truth is the light of the face — life, joy, as explained (<span class="lr">LM I:23</span>). The essential joy is through the point of truth in the Jewish heart — his soul knowing the holiness of Israel's faith, all our joy: <span class="v">"I shall rejoice in Hashem"</span>; <span class="v">"in Him our hearts rejoice"</span>; <span class="v">"let Israel rejoice in its Maker."</span> Every person, if he reminds himself he is of the seed of Israel, can gladden himself wherever he is.</div>

<div class="p">But the <span class="h">ba'al davar</span> provokes exceedingly on this point — first enticing to sin, distracting with money and livelihood, then overpowering with melancholy, especially when one is aroused to return to Hashem. As explained (<span class="lr">LM II:48</span>): <span class="mx">"as soon as a person wants to draw close to Hashem, it is a great sin to have sadness."</span> The essential exile of Israel, the exile of the <span class="h">Shechinah</span>, is sadness.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He saw he could not prevail against him"</span> — against Yaakov himself he had no power, for he was exceedingly holy in guarding the <span class="h">bris</span> — the very essence of joy, the very essence of truth. But due to our many sins he <span class="v">"touched the hollow of his thigh"</span> — affecting his children, the later generations (= the feet, <span class="h">ikvesa d'Meshicha</span>). Their essential overpowering is in the feet where the <span class="h">klipos</span> cling — sadness, the side of death: <span class="v">"her feet descend."</span> From this derives: <span class="v">"the children of Israel do not eat the sciatic nerve"</span> — the aspect of <span class="h">Tisha B'Av</span>, the destruction caused by needless weeping: <span class="v">"the people wept that night"</span> — <span class="mx">"you wept for nothing; I shall establish a weeping for generations."</span></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"He said: 'Send me away, for dawn has risen.' He said: 'I shall not send you unless you bless me.'"</span> The man supposed: since he touched Yaakov's thigh, Yaakov would release him. But Yaakov said: <span class="v">"I shall not send you unless you bless me"</span> — as Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes on <span class="v">"gladness and joy shall they attain, and sorrow and sighing shall flee"</span>: the sorrow and sighing want to flee when one overpowers with joy, but one must seize them and force them into the joy.</div>

<div class="p">The angel of Esav wanted to leave when dawn arose — seeing every Jew seizing <span class="h">tzitzis</span> and <span class="h">tefillin</span> with joy, reciting <span class="h">Pesukay d'Zimrah</span> and praises with joy. Through this, the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>'s power raises holy sparks from the Chambers of Exchange. He said: <span class="mx">"send me away — my time to sing has arrived."</span> All the angels sing with joy — their entire vitality. But many angels accuse man: <span class="v">"what is man..."</span> — unworthy of singing because sunken in this world of desires (= sadness). But they do not know that on the contrary: this is the essential song and joy of Hashem — when joy ascends from this World of Action full of sadness, when people transform sorrow specifically to gladness and joy.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Yaakov told him: <span class="v">"I shall not send you"</span> — "You want to ascend and sing (= joy), while here you want to cast my children into sadness? I seize you against your will — <span class="v">'unless you bless me'</span> (= joy). <span class="v">'The blessing of Hashem enriches, and He adds no sadness with it.'</span> I seize you to transform you to joy — you yourself shall gladden them": <span class="v">"gladness and joy shall they attain, and sorrow and sighing shall flee"</span>; <span class="v">"when Hashem favors a man's ways, even his enemies make peace with him"</span>; <span class="v">"they shall bring all your brethren as an offering to Hashem"</span> — the nations themselves transformed to gladden Israel. Seizing sorrow and sighing to transform to joy: <span class="v">"I shall not send you unless you bless me."</span></div>

<div class="p">It is brought: "Now you cannot sing until Israel sings first": <span class="v">"when the morning stars sing, then all the angels shout"</span> — Israel first. "My holiness has begun — from now on you cannot sing until my children sing first. I seize you until you bless me — you yourself will transform to gladden my children." This is the essential complete sorting — exchanging evil for good, transforming sorrow to joy. Through this one walks and makes His G-dliness known in all worlds — the <span class="h">tikun</span> of <span class="h">Netzach-Hod-Yesod</span> (= the songs and praises of Israel) — ascending to <span class="h">Keser</span>, where Yaakov ascends. When Israel sings with joy, then the angel can sing too. Specifically through transforming sorrow to joy — <span class="v">"I shall not send you unless you bless me."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 26 — The Name Yisrael = <i>Shir Kel</i>: Song to G-d</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Your name shall no longer be Yaakov, but Yisrael, for you have striven with G-d and with men, and prevailed."</span> He conceded: "No longer Yaakov" (implying battle with the feet: <span class="v">"his hand grasped Esav's heel"</span>), "but Yisrael" — he already won: <span class="v">"you have striven with G-d and with men, and prevailed."</span></div>

<div class="p">Through the joy of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> one ascends to <span class="h">Keser</span>. The mind strikes the <span class="h">Prisah</span>, perceiving the nine chambers — but only through <span class="h">mi yaimar</span>, descending to the Chambers of Exchange. <span class="v">"You have striven with G-d"</span> — the supernal <span class="h">tzimtzum</span>, <span class="h">Keser</span> (also called <span class="h">Elokim</span>, per the Arizal). When the pursuit strikes the obstructer — yet he overpowers, drawing the nine chambers: like a battle. <span class="v">"And with men"</span> — Esav and Lavan (= the Chambers of Exchange) — <span class="v">"and you prevailed."</span> Impossible to strive with <span class="h">G-d</span> except by striving with men — overpowering to sort holiness from there. The name <span class="h">Yisrael</span> is <span class="h">shir Kel</span> — song to G-d — song and joy. The essential prevailing is through joy.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 27 — "The Sun Rose for Him": The Hidden Light</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"The sun rose for him — to heal him from his limp."</span> Our Sages say the future sun illuminated for him: <span class="v">"the sun of righteousness shall rise with healing"</span> — the hidden light (holy Zohar). This is the light perceived through the joy of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> (= Yaakov's holiness). One ascends to <span class="h">Keser</span>, perceiving light in <span class="h">mati v'lo mati</span>. This is the hidden light; all intellectual lights derive from there. The great <span class="h">tzadikim</span> merit this even now. One depends on the other: more joy of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> = more lights; more lights = more joy. Yaakov merited the sun in its full force — the hidden light — until healed from his limp (= his descendants in later generations, where sadness overpowers). Through the intensity of this light, he healed his descendants — their healing through joy drawn from the source of joy (<span class="v">"eternal joy upon their heads"</span>). All our strength in the depth of exile is only through the point of joy the great <span class="h">tzadikim</span> draw upon us — <span class="v">"the sun rose for him to heal his limp."</span> This is <span class="h">"aisu ashli u'moshchu"</span> — drawing joy from the source that will be revealed in the future. This is the boast: he could heal the King's daughter through joy.</div>

<div class="p">Yaakov went back for small vessels — small sparks to raise and sort. The essential perception is through <span class="h">mi yaimar</span> — sorting sparks from the Chambers of Exchange.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 28 — The Small Flask: The Anointing Oil and the Chanukah Miracle</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">pach</span> [flask] alludes to the flask of oil — <span class="v">"he poured oil upon its top"</span>: the <span class="h">tzapachas hashemen</span> that will not be depleted, the anointing oil in which blessing resided. From it were anointed <span class="h">Kohanim</span>, kings, and vessels of service — all enduring for the future. All this is the <span class="h">Chanukah</span>-oil: the miracle — oil for one day burning eight days, for the above blessing resided in it. Yaakov labored to draw upon Israel this blessing of the oil (= the blessing of intellect). The angel grew jealous and provoked him — Yaakov vanquished him, compelling him to bless: he himself transformed to blessing (= joy), until the above light shone (= the hidden light).</div>

<div class="sn">§ 29 — The <i>Kavanos</i> of Chanukah: <i>Ehyeh</i> × <i>Ehyeh</i> = <i>Emes</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the <span class="h">kavanos</span> of <span class="h">Chanukah</span>: intend each night the Name <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> × <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> (= <span class="h">Emes</span>), arousing one <span class="h">midah</span> from the thirteen <span class="h">Mechilin d'Rachamay</span>, up to <span class="h">Notzair</span> [Guards (Chesed)]; the Name <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> in a unique permutation each night — three <span class="h">Ehyeh</span>'s with <span class="h">yuddin</span>, <span class="h">heh</span>'s, <span class="h">alephs</span>; see there.</div>

<div class="p">The essential <span class="h">kavanah</span>: draw the joy of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> from the World to Come into this world. Remember the ultimate World to Come — nothing will remain except the point of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span>. Therefore, when performing any <span class="h">mitzvah</span>, overpower to do it with immense joy — only this is eternal vitality. Even if he did what he did — rejoice even more. On the contrary: he should rejoice that he too, in his lowliness, merits wrapping in <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, donning <span class="h">tefillin</span>, giving <span class="h">tzedakah</span>: <span class="v">"gladness and joy shall they attain, and sorrow and sighing shall flee"</span> — seizing sorrow and bringing it into joy (Hilchos Periyah v'Riviyah 4). All drawn through kindling the <span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span> — drawing <span class="h">Shabbos</span>-joy into the weekdays (<span class="lr">LM II:2</span>).</div>

<div class="p">All merited through truth (= Yaakov, the essence of joy). The truth in the heart knows nothing will remain except the <span class="h">mitzvah</span>. <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> × <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> = <span class="h">Emes</span>. <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> is <span class="h">Keser</span> — the Arranger and Settler. There is the source of joy: <span class="v">"eternal joy upon their heads."</span> There is the root of the oil-light — <span class="h">Keser</span>: <span class="v">"the crown of his G-d upon his head."</span> From there all oil-lights are drawn — the light of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>. He illuminates in concealment through the great <span class="h">tzadikim</span> — implanting truth so we rejoice in <span class="h">mitzvos</span> even now. The <span class="h">Chanukah</span>-oil light derives from the <span class="h">Kohain Gadol</span> anointed with the anointing oil. (Even though in the Second <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> the anointing oil was hidden — the <span class="h">Kohain Gadol</span>'s holiness derives from Aharon who was anointed.)</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Send Your light and Your truth — they shall guide me; bring me to Your holy mountain"</span> (= the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, the nine chambers); <span class="v">"I shall come to the G-d of my joyful exultation"</span> — meriting joy. All through the light of truth (= the light of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>). The <span class="h">Chanukah</span>-oil light illuminates the point of truth in the heart — drawing the holiness of the nine chambers, where the source of joy is. <span class="v">"I shall thank You"</span> — thanksgiving.</div>

<div class="p">The three permutations of <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> total <span class="h">chosam</span> [seal] in <span class="h">gematria</span> — the seal on the <span class="h">Chanukah</span>-oil, sealed with the <span class="h">Kohain Gadol</span>'s seal. The essential seal is truth: <span class="mx">"the seal of the Holy One is truth."</span> <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> is the <span class="h">Prisah</span> and obstructer — a seal sealing off the mind, obstructing until it settles; through this specifically the essential perception. The essential totality of all perceptions is truth — the essential wisdom is truth, especially in perceiving G-dliness. Every person's essential perception is the ultimate knowledge that we do not know — only drawing <span class="h">emunah</span> (= truth). By seeing the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>'s perceptions, truth and <span class="h">emunah</span> are strengthened in every Jewish heart. The essential light (= <span class="h">menorah</span>-oil, the <span class="h">Chanukah</span> miracle) is drawn through the seal (= the obstructer). Therefore the miracle was through oil sealed with the <span class="h">Kohain Gadol</span>'s seal.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Ehyeh</span> is <span class="h">Ana zamin l'mehevay</span> [I am prepared to be] — the joy in the heart: in the end, certainly some being will emerge from me. All existence now is emptiness — especially since one must die. This is no existence. Only: <span class="h">"Ana zamin l'mehevay"</span> — I am destined for eternal existence. As I heard from his holy mouth <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> regarding strengthening with joy. All that endures is the point of the <span class="h">mitzvos</span>. This is <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> — the essential joy.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"What are we, what are our lives"</span> etc. — everything is emptiness, no existence except the point of Torah and <span class="h">mitzvos</span>. Therefore we say: <span class="v">"fortunate are we"</span> — the joy of Israel's holiness, unifying His Name daily: the joy of <span class="h">mitzvos</span>, for <span class="v">"all Your commandments are faith."</span></div>

<div class="p">The unique permutation each night — to rectify the Chambers of Exchange, overpowering with lies, reversals, and exchanges (evil musings). Each time through <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> × <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> in a unique permutation (each equaling <span class="h">Emes</span>). According to the overpowering of their changes, one must draw truth — through good counsel, various changes for good: Torah, <span class="h">tefilah</span>, conversation — all from the permutations of <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> (= truth). One must transform everything for good. According to the sadness of the Chambers of Exchange, transform everything to joy — sins transformed to merits: <span class="v">"on that day the sin of Israel will be sought, and it will be gone."</span> Each day unique permutations of <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> (= truth) according to the sorting needed. Truth is one, but from the receivers' side — many variations for good (<span class="lr">LM I:251</span>). The <span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span> (= the light of truth) requires a unique permutation each day.</div>

<div class="p">This is intending to draw the thirteen <span class="h">Mechilin d'Rachamay</span>. Through the thirteen <span class="h">midos</span> of mercy, sins are transformed to merits (= joy): <span class="v">"gladness and joy shall they attain"</span> — the <span class="h">Chanukah</span> miracle: the <span class="h">tzadikim</span> transform everything to joy, and every person can draw this light — the <span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 30 — Kindling from Nightfall Until "the Foot Ceases": The Moon's Blemish</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span> is kindled from the stars' emergence until the foot ceases from the marketplace. The essential sadness — the exile of the <span class="h">Shechinah</span> — derives from the moon's blemish. The luminaries are joy; originally both were great; through the moon's accusation it was diminished: <span class="v">"let there be luminaries"</span> [deficiently]. From this the sustenance of sadness is drawn: <span class="mx">"'luminaries' — this is Lilis"</span> — all wailing, sadness, and melancholy (= darkness). Israel labors to fill the moon's blemish — through <span class="h">mitzvos</span> with joy. Specifically through the joy of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span>, the moon's blemish is repaired.</div>

<div class="p">The custom is to sanctify the moon with great joy — dances at <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span>: <span class="mx">"joyful and glad to fulfill."</span> <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span> fills the moon's blemish, sanctified with joy — the essential <span class="h">tikun</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Israel counts by the moon — the lesser luminary: <span class="v">"you are the fewest"</span> — <span class="mx">"you diminish yourselves when I bestow good"</span> — the praise of the <span class="h">tzadikim</span>, each called small: <span class="mx">"Yaakov the small, David the small."</span> The essential joy is through smallness, lowliness, and humility: <span class="v">"the humble shall increase joy in Hashem."</span></div>

<div class="p">The nations' joy is through pride — attaining wealth, they become haughty. Their joy is no joy — always mixed: <span class="v">"of laughter — madness; of joy — what does it accomplish?"</span> No joy in worldly affairs. Their joy is the laughter of the fool — sadness (holy Zohar; <span class="lr">LM I:23</span>): <span class="v">"the end of joy is sorrow."</span> No one fulfills desires through wealth: <span class="mx">"no one dies with half his desires."</span> Through greatness — no joy; all turns to sorrow.</div>

<div class="p">But the joy of the <span class="h">tzadikim</span> — the joy of Israel — is through smallness. So small that whatever they receive, they rejoice. Even with suffering, they rejoice — thanking Hashem in good and severity: <span class="v">"in Hashem I shall praise the word; in G-d I shall praise the word."</span> They rejoice in their portion, knowing even the little is undeserved kindness. Their eternal joy — the joy of <span class="h">mitzvos</span>. The smaller they are, the more they overpower to rejoice: despite everything, he merits a <span class="h">mitzvah</span> — <span class="v">"gladness and joy shall they attain."</span></div>

<div class="p">Hashem comforted the moon: <span class="mx">"tzadikim will be called by your name."</span> Her consolation is joy — <span class="h">tzadikim</span> called small in her name, all their joy through smallness, enduring forever. He gave her the stars: <span class="v">"those who bring the many to righteousness — like the stars"</span> — the <span class="h">tzadikim</span> who merit the many by implanting joy, finding good points in each person: <span class="v">"yet a little while and there is no wicked person"</span> — <span class="v">"I shall sing to my G-d while I yet live."</span> Stars — illuminating points gladdening Israel, filling the moon with light.</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">Ner Chanukah</span> is kindled from the stars' emergence — <span class="v">"those who bring the many to righteousness — like the stars"</span> — until the foot ceases from the marketplace: the essential <span class="h">tikun</span> through joy — raising the feet from the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>'s hold (= sadness). Through joy, <span class="h">Malchus</span> is raised, the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> arouses all worlds — the ascent of the feet from the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>'s sustenance.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 31 — David's Dance Before the Ark: Smallness = True Joy</div>

<div class="p">David's reply to Michal: <span class="v">"how honored was the king of Israel today!"</span> (Shmuel II:6) — he humbled himself greatly, leaping and dancing with immense joy when bringing the Ark. He answered: <span class="v">"before Hashem who chose me over your father... I shall become even more abased."</span> On the contrary — this is the intensity of my joy, because I am truly so small in my eyes. Through this Hashem chose me as king. As our Sages say (Yoma 22): <span class="mx">"a leader is not appointed unless a basket of vermin hangs behind him."</span> Shaul's kingship did not endure — he had no blemish. The essential ascent of holy <span class="h">Malchus</span> is through joy — specifically through humility, like David: <span class="v">"I am a worm and not a man."</span> In this he would gladden himself — that despite everything, Hashem bestowed such kindnesses.</div>

<div class="p">So every Jew — the more they distance him from joy because of his lowliness, the more he must strengthen himself to be joyful through this specifically. Despite everything, I am clothed in <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, I recite <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> every day. This is filling the moon's blemish — the kingship of David enduring forever. During <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span> we exclaim: <span class="mx">"David King of Israel lives and endures."</span> The essential eternal vitality is joy — merited through closeness to <span class="h">tzadikim</span>: <span class="v">"You shall make known to me the path of life; fullness of joys is Your countenance."</span> David is the totality of Israel's joy, the <span class="h">badcha d'malka</span> (holy Zohar), who merited the ten types of melody. The essential <span class="h">tikun</span> of the moon's blemish is through joy — David, who merited holy <span class="h">Malchus</span> forever.</div>

<div class="p">Our Sages say: <span class="mx">"even if Israel merited nothing more than greeting their Father in Heaven once a month, it would suffice."</span> This is the essential holiness of Israel — in this transient world, rejoicing in the joy of holy <span class="h">emunah</span> — <span class="h">Kiddush Levanah</span>. All the more since we perform many <span class="h">mitzvos</span> daily and unify His Name twice daily.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 32 — Yaakov, Yosef, and the Flame That Consumes All Obstacles</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Yaakov settled in the land of his father's sojournings"</span>; <span class="v">"these are the generations of Yaakov — Yosef."</span> Our Sages (Midrash Rabbah): <span class="v">"sojournings"</span> = converts — Yaakov converted converts. It is brought (<span class="lr">LM I:228</span>): <span class="mx">"Yaakov sought tranquility — the fury of Yosef leaped upon him."</span> One who converts converts will have suffering and dispute. So every person — those returning to Hashem through the <span class="h">tzadik</span> face dispute, suffering, and provocation: impossible to draw close without this (<span class="lr">LM I:72</span>).</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">tikun</span>: Yosef himself. Rashi: <span class="mx">"the flax-dealer — his camels entered laden with flax. The coal-seller wondered. A clever one: one spark from your bellows burns all the flax. 'The house of Yaakov fire, the house of Yosef flame, the house of Esav straw' — one spark from Yosef consumes everything."</span></div>

<div class="p">Yosef is the true <span class="h">tzadik</span> who gladdens every Jewish heart, transforming sorrow to joy — igniting hearts to Hashem (<span class="lr">LM II:9</span>): <span class="mx">"a man in whom there is spirit"</span> — blowing the dust (= sadness) from the Jewish heart. This is Yosef: <span class="v">"can there be found such a man, in whom the spirit of G-d resides?"</span></div>

<div class="p">Yosef descends into all the Chambers of Exchange, extracting every soul — whoever wishes to cling to him. (One who does not wish — impossible to help: <span class="v">"speak not in a fool's ears."</span>) But whoever desires life — the <span class="h">tzadik</span> can extract him. Yosef descended: <span class="v">"sold as a slave"</span> — slavery (= sadness), from the contamination of the serpent. He had immense trials, was imprisoned for years. He passed through all the Chambers of Exchange, emerged in peace — meriting immense additional holiness: <span class="h">Yosef</span> [= addition]: <span class="mx">"a wise man hears and adds."</span></div>

<div class="p">Rachel's prophecy at his birth: <span class="v">"G-d has gathered my shame"</span> — through the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, all disgraces are nullified. <span class="v">"May Hashem add another son"</span> — he transforms disgraces to honor, sorrow to joy: good deeds gladdening the heart (<span class="mx">"a wise son gladdens a father"</span>; <span class="mx">"the offspring of the righteous are good deeds"</span>). Through the disgraces specifically — adding joy. This is Yosef: <span class="v">"G-d sent me for sustenance"</span>; <span class="v">"you intended evil; G-d intended good, to sustain a great people."</span> It is stated: <span class="mx">"fortunate are the ba'alay teshuvah — G-d sent them for sustenance"</span> — the descent for the sake of ascent, everything transformed to joy.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Yaakov settled"</span> — the Arranger and Settler (the intellect = Yaakov). <span class="v">"In his father's sojournings"</span> — converting converts (= <span class="h">mi yaimar</span>). But each time they provoke him. The <span class="h">tikun</span>: <span class="v">"the generations of Yaakov — Yosef"</span> — the <span class="h">tzadik</span> gives birth to Yosef — additional holiness each time, never falling into the old age of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>. <span class="v">"The house of Yosef a flame"</span> — igniting Yaakov's fire. <span class="v">"A man in whom the spirit of G-d resides"</span> — blowing dust from every Jew. One spark from Yosef burns all the chieftains of Esav — all obstacles, sadness, and provocation. Through one spark of truth implanted in the Jewish heart — all obstructers consumed.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 33 — "A Son of Old Age": Yosef Conquers the Old Age of the <i>Sitra Achra</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Israel loved Yosef more than all his sons, for he was a son of old age to him"</span> — <span class="v">"old age"</span> in the plural. He constantly overpowers the holy old age over the old age of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> — which works to make a person fall into old age (= weakening his mind). Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> warned: <span class="mx">"it is forbidden to be old."</span> Subdued through the old man of holiness — <span class="mx">"an elder who acquired wisdom"</span> (= Yosef, adding holiness each time; see Hilchos Tefillin 5).</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"A son of old age"</span> — in the plural: each time adding holy old age upon holy old age: <span class="v">"fear of Hashem adds days"</span> — subduing the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>'s old age. David prayed: <span class="v">"do not cast me away in old age."</span> One must renew each time: <span class="v">"those who hope in Hashem shall renew their strength"</span> — Yosef the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, named for adding holiness and <span class="h">da'as</span> (= vitality) each time.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 34 — Yaakov and Yosef = 13 × <i>Havayah</i>: The Thirteen <i>Midos</i> of Mercy</div>

<div class="p">Yaakov and Yosef together equal thirteen times the Name <span class="h">Havayah</span>. The <span class="h">kavanos</span> of <span class="h">Chanukah</span> draw the thirteen <span class="h">Tikunai Dikna</span> (= the thirteen <span class="h">midos</span> of mercy). The root of the three unifications equaling <span class="h">Ner</span> is the supernal unification <span class="h">Havayah</span>-<span class="h">Ehyeh</span> (Peri Eitz Chaim).</div>

<div class="p">The foundation of all Names is the Name <span class="h">Havayah</span> — the very essence of truth: <span class="v">"the truth of Hashem is forever."</span> All unifications through <span class="h">mitzvos</span> correspond to sorting holy sparks from the <span class="h">klipos</span> (= <span class="h">mi yaimar</span>). The essential thing: strengthening in truth and <span class="h">emunah</span> in Hashem, His Torah, and His true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> — who reveal the holiness of every <span class="h">mitzvah</span> (our life and eternal sustenance), until we merit performing the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> with joy. Through this — the ascent of the <span class="h">Shechinah</span> from exile until the nine chambers are fashioned. The essential thing is the point of truth — <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> × <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> = <span class="h">Emes</span>.</div>

<div class="p">To draw this truth requires the Name <span class="h">Havayah</span> unified with <span class="h">Ehyeh</span>. Accomplished through the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> (= Yaakov and Yosef), illuminating truth in every Jewish heart, blowing away the dust (= sadness) until the heart burns for Hashem. The root of this holy fire is Yaakov: <span class="v">"the house of Yaakov fire."</span> The inflaming through Yosef: <span class="v">"the house of Yosef flame"</span> — burning for Hashem: <span class="v">"sparks of fire, a flame of G-d"</span> — until <span class="v">"many waters cannot quench the love."</span> <span class="v">"If a man would give all his wealth for love"</span> — trying to divert from truth through wealth (where sadness clings: <span class="mx">"more possessions, more worry"</span>) — <span class="v">"they would utterly despise him."</span> For he has tasted the pleasantness of truth through the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span>.</div>

<div class="p">All this in the eight days of <span class="h">Chanukah</span>: kindle each night, drawing the holy fire from Yaakov and Yosef. Yaakov began drawing the holy anointing oil (oaseyos kaf-daled, kaf-ches). Yosef is <span class="h">Mashiach ben Yosef</span> — descending into the depths of the <span class="h">klipos</span>, meriting the nine chambers where the oil's root resides.</div>

<div class="p">Yaakov and Yosef equal thirteen times <span class="h">Havayah</span> — the power of the great mercy. <span class="h">Havayah</span> is the essence of mercy: <span class="v">"Hashem, Hashem, G-d compassionate and gracious."</span> Their drawing upon us is through the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span>, illuminating truth — <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> × <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> = <span class="h">Emes</span>.</div>

<div class="p">In the <span class="h">kavanos</span>: each night, one <span class="h">Ehyeh</span> and one <span class="h">midah</span> of the thirteen <span class="h">Tikunai Dikna</span>. Until the eighth night — <span class="h">Notzair</span> [Guards (Chesed)] (after <span class="h">v'Emes</span>), where the remaining <span class="h">tikunim</span> through <span class="h">v'Nakeh</span> are encompassed. The essence of truth is Yaakov: <span class="v">"grant truth to Yaakov."</span> Yaakov equals seven times <span class="h">Havayah</span> — seven <span class="h">Tikunai Dikna</span> through <span class="h">v'Emes</span>, the seventh <span class="h">tikun</span>. The eighth — <span class="h">Notzair</span> [Guards (Chesed)] — is Yosef, who inflames truth. When one reaches the eighth night (= Yosef's <span class="h">tikun</span>, the inflaming of truth), all remaining <span class="h">tikunim</span> are encompassed — no further open kindling needed. The essential engagement was drawing Yaakov's truth until reaching Yosef who inflames it. The remaining <span class="h">tikunim</span> encompassed in concealment.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 35 — Yosef = <i>Mashiach</i>: The Completion Cannot Yet Be Revealed</div>

<div class="p">Yosef is <span class="h">Mashiach</span>, who will complete the <span class="h">ge'ulah</span> (= truth): <span class="v">"send Your light and Your truth."</span> But the complete revelation of truth cannot now be illuminated in the open: <span class="mx">"the heart does not reveal to the mouth."</span> Also, the light should not be inflamed excessively: <span class="v">"lest they break through"</span> (<span class="lr">LM II:9</span>), and as in this <span class="h">Torah</span> regarding the Arranger and Settler.</div>

<div class="p">At the eighth night — Yosef's <span class="h">tikun</span> (Yosef equaling six times <span class="h">Havayah</span>) — one draws one Name (after the seven times <span class="h">Havayah</span> = Yaakov in the first seven nights). It is impossible to illuminate further. The remaining <span class="h">Tikunai Dikna</span> are encompassed in concealment — impossible now to reveal more.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 36 — Closing: All Our Vitality Through the Mercy the <i>Tzadikim</i> Draw Upon Us</div>

<div class="p">All our vitality and sustenance is through the very essence of the great mercy the true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> draw upon us — through the thirteen <span class="h">midos</span> of mercy (= the thirteen <span class="h">Tikunai Dikna</span>). Through this they illuminate the point of truth in each person's heart, wherever he is — so he too can be aroused and inflamed for Hashem with sparks of the flame of G-d — until he too gladdens his soul. Through this comes his essential ascent. All this is the aspect of <span class="h">Chanukah</span>. Blessed is Hashem forever, <span class="h">amain</span> and <span class="h">amain</span>.</div>

